.TH PEITERM 1 "2026-09-29" "Peios"
.SH NAME
peiterm \- GXWI terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peiterm
.RI [ directory ]
.br
.B peiterm
.I program
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens a window on the GXWI desktop with a shell in it, on a pseudoterminal.
The shell is the one named by
.B SHELL
in the environment, or
.I /bin/sh
if none is named, and it is started in the home directory of whoever logged on.
.PP
Given one argument that is a directory, the shell is started there instead.
Given anything else, the first argument is run in place of the shell and the
rest are passed to it.
.PP
The terminal belongs to the program and not to the browser showing it: a page
that is closed and opened again, or another device looking at the same
session, is shown the terminal as it stands.
.PP
The window closes when the shell ends. Closing the window hangs the terminal
up on whatever is running in it.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy what is selected.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+V, Shift+Insert
Paste.
.PP
The desktop's own chords are the desktop's while the keyboard is in the
terminal.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
Set to
.I xterm-256color
for what is started.
.TP
.B GXWI_DISPLAY
Names the desktop. It is left in the environment of what is started, so a
program run from the terminal can open windows of its own.
.SH NOTES
Runs within a GXWI session. Its parent supplies the session descriptors and
identity; launch it through the desktop.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Peios learn documentation.
